#!/bin/sh
# do-screenshot — take a screenshot of the X11 desktop, an area or the
# active window, save it as PNG and copy it to the clipboard
# usage: do-screenshot [-d dir] [desktop|area|window|delay [seconds]]
#
#   desktop  the whole X screen, every output
#   area     a rectangle or a window picked with the mouse
#   window   the window that has the focus
#   delay    the window that has the focus N seconds from now (default
#            5), time to switch to it; counted down in notifications
# Without a mode, one is picked from a rofi menu, so a key binding or a
# bar button can run it bare (i3: bindsym --release Print exec
# --no-startup-id do-screenshot); a menu dismissed is not an error.
#
# The file is <dir>/Screenshot_YYYY-MM-DD-HH-MM-SS.png, dir being -d,
# else $XDG_PICTURES_DIR, else ~/Pictures; a name already taken gets a
# -2, -3... suffix.  Its path is printed on stdout.  It is copied to the
# clipboard with xclip and announced with notify-send, each skipped with
# a word on stderr when missing.
# Exit status: 0 success or menu dismissed, 1 failure (an area selection
# cancelled included), 2 usage error.
# 'local' is not POSIX, but every shell this runs under has it
# shellcheck disable=SC3043
set -eu

prog=${0##*/}
readonly app=screenshot default_delay=5

# maim, xdotool, xclip, notify-send and rofi live in /usr/local/bin on
# FreeBSD, which is not on every window manager's PATH.
PATH=$PATH:/usr/local/bin

usage() {
    printf 'usage: %s [-d dir] [desktop|area|window|delay [seconds]]\n' "$prog"
    printf '  -d dir  save into dir\n'
    # shellcheck disable=SC2016  # the variable's name, not its value
    printf '          (default: $XDG_PICTURES_DIR, else ~/Pictures)\n'
    printf '  without a mode, pick one from a rofi menu\n'
}

die() {
    printf '%s: %s\n' "$prog" "$*" >&2
    exit 1
}

have() {
    command -v "$1" > /dev/null 2>&1
}

# menu — print the mode picked from rofi, nothing when dismissed
menu() {
    local chosen
    have rofi || die "no mode given and no rofi to ask for one"
    chosen=$(printf '%s\n' 'Desktop' 'Area' 'Window' 'Window, delayed' |
        rofi -dmenu -i -p Screenshot 2> /dev/null) || chosen=
    case $chosen in
    Desktop) printf 'desktop\n' ;;
    Area) printf 'area\n' ;;
    Window) printf 'window\n' ;;
    'Window, delayed') printf 'delay\n' ;;
    esac
}

# notify ARG... — notify-send, its notification id (with -p) on stdout;
# silent and successful without it
notify() {
    have notify-send || return 0
    notify-send -a "$app" "$@" 2> /dev/null || :
}

# countdown SECONDS — wait, counting down in a notification replaced
# each second; sets nid to that notification's id, if it gave one
countdown() {
    local seconds="$1" i="$1" id
    nid=
    if ! have notify-send; then
        sleep "$seconds"
        return 0
    fi
    while [ "$i" -gt 0 ]; do
        id=$(notify -p ${nid:+-r "$nid"} -t 1100 \
            -h "int:value:$(((seconds - i) * 100 / seconds))" Screenshot \
            "Capturing the active window in ${i}s; switch to it now.")
        nid=${id:-$nid}
        sleep 1
        i=$((i - 1))
    done
    notify ${nid:+-r "$nid"} -t 800 -h int:value:100 Screenshot \
        'Capturing now' > /dev/null
    sleep 0.5
}

active_window() {
    have xdotool || die "xdotool is needed to find the active window"
    xdotool getactivewindow 2> /dev/null ||
        die "xdotool cannot tell the active window"
}

# markup TEXT — TEXT with &, < and > escaped for a notification body
markup() {
    printf '%s' "$1" | sed 's/&/\&amp;/g; s/</\&lt;/g; s/>/\&gt;/g'
}

dir=${XDG_PICTURES_DIR:-$HOME/Pictures}
while getopts d:h opt; do
    case $opt in
    d) dir=$OPTARG ;;
    h) usage; exit 0 ;;
    *) usage >&2; exit 2 ;;
    esac
done
shift $((OPTIND - 1))

delay=
case $# in
0) mode= ;;
1) mode=$1 ;;
2)
    mode=$1 delay=$2
    case $mode:$delay in
    delay:*[!0-9]* | delay: | delay:0) usage >&2; exit 2 ;;
    delay:*) ;;
    *) usage >&2; exit 2 ;;
    esac
    ;;
*) usage >&2; exit 2 ;;
esac
case $mode in
'' | desktop | area | window | delay) ;;
*) usage >&2; exit 2 ;;
esac

if [ -z "$mode" ]; then
    mode=$(menu)
    [ -n "$mode" ] || exit 0
fi

have maim || die "maim is not installed"
mkdir -p -- "$dir" || die "cannot create $dir"
base=$dir/Screenshot_$(date +%Y-%m-%d-%H-%M-%S)
file=$base.png
n=1
while [ -e "$file" ]; do
    n=$((n + 1))
    file=$base-$n.png
done

nid=
case $mode in
desktop) set -- ;;
area) set -- -s ;;
window)
    win=$(active_window)
    set -- -i "$win"
    ;;
delay)
    countdown "${delay:-$default_delay}"
    win=$(active_window)
    set -- -i "$win"
    ;;
esac
if ! maim -u -f png "$@" "$file"; then
    rm -f -- "$file"
    die "maim took no screenshot"
fi

if ! have xclip; then
    printf '%s: no xclip, so not copied to the clipboard\n' "$prog" >&2
    copied='Saved'
elif xclip -selection clipboard -t image/png -i "$file" 2> /dev/null; then
    copied='Copied to the clipboard and saved'
else
    printf '%s: xclip could not copy it to the clipboard\n' "$prog" >&2
    copied='Saved'
fi
if have notify-send; then
    link="<a href=\"file://$(markup "$file")\">$(markup "${file##*/}")</a>"
    notify ${nid:+-r "$nid"} -h "string:image-path:$file" Screenshot \
        "$copied as $link" > /dev/null
else
    printf '%s: no notify-send, so not announced\n' "$prog" >&2
fi
printf '%s\n' "$file"
